id: pm-gh1534
title: "GH-1534: retain root relationship evidence before optional context detail"
description: "Reproduce GH-1534 on the SDK deps context surface. Bounded relationship packing retains optional nodes while dropping root blocking and parent edges. Preserve decision evidence and disclose omissions. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1534"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T16:30:07.371Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:17.212Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:16.144Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:16.144Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Direct root relationships and endpoints precede optional sibling detail; Infeasible evidence is reported within the token ceiling; SDK CLI and MCP share packing and omission contracts
parent: pm-gh1361
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "Order direct prerequisite and ancestor endpoints before optional context, reserve root-edge costs, skip unaffordable edges while retaining omission counts, and bind cursor continuation to the required-evidence packing policy."
expected_result: "Required root endpoints precede optional descendants and feasible later edges survive an oversized edge, with stable producer pages and explicit bounded omissions."
actual_result: "The three review regressions fail on the first head and pass after remediation. All70 linked graph/dependency cases pass, including root ordering, cursor continuity, stale-policy rejection and oversized-edge accounting. Typecheck lint SDK surface and documentation checks pass. Final hosted static and coverage remain required; failed local startup admissions remain recorded."
