comments[11]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T16:30:07.371Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: strict full all-status read inspected 3042/3042 items including 2766 closed with no omissions. No GH-1534 owner exists. Closed pm-8kch fixes missing references while pm-gh1361 owns broader semantic coverage. GitHub open PR and security-alert inventories are empty."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T16:30:40.002Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation plan: reserve root-edge costs alongside each direct endpoint in the reusable relationship kernel, keep direct edges first under edge limits, and disclose producer truncation in the shared read-output omission receipt. Add SDK kernel and actual CLI/MCP budget regressions before the fix."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T16:38:40.285Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Regression sensitivity: unchanged final context-evidence tests copied to isolated detached base 13c19fe9 fail all 3 cases. Kernel and real adapter assertions fail because root blocker/parent edges disappear. Corrected current tree passes all 3. Existing graph/context/deps suite passed 108 cases before the run-fixture timestamp correction. Both PM owners are the only in_progress items. New documentation explains bounded evidence and matching active test denominators."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T16:48:40.677Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Read-only operations/security inventory: all open GitHub issues have canonical PM-link comments after intaking GH1534/1535. GH1528 was closed against the live shipped fix in PR1531 and its existing issue evidence. pnpm audit reports0 vulnerabilities across569 dependencies, and GitHub security-alert inventories are empty. Latest pm-changelog2026.10.21 is installed and its initial check passes. Existing release/nightly and dependency-cooldown owners receive fresh evidence without implementation claims."
    edited_at: "2026-10-21T17:33:47.935Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T17:04:01.851Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Local verification limitation retained: full run has10972 passing tests but3 failures (two concurrency-sensitive deadlines and one npm module discovery prerequisite), so no whole-suite or coverage success is claimed. The unchanged focused27-case graph/evidence runner passes after the full run. The final kernel refactor extracts node projection to satisfy the existing cognitive-complexity ceiling while retaining its behavior; final linked tests and static gates follow. Canonical host qualification evidence is recorded on pm-bj7rq0, which remains open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T17:18:05.132Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Static preflight found missing intake metadata on the two new progressive items: risk, confidence, estimate and expected outcome were absent, and this item had only its parent relationship. Added explicit estimates and evidence-based risk/confidence with expected outcomes. Linked the paired test-population issue as related because both fixes share the SDK context-integrity acceptance surface. No thresholds or enforcement contracts were changed. The confidence unit is a documented integer percentage (90), not a fraction. Re-run the exact tracker-context assurance and remaining static stages before closure."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T17:34:11.505Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final local source/static contracts pass through registry/OSV evidence, lint, exports, contracts, SDK/package parity, grammar/recovery/token checks, tracker-context assurance and SDK import-cost admission. Remaining graph/record assurance and mutation controls are verified separately. The complete static command retains a qualified local CLI transport-floor failure; no budget is raised and final hosted static and coverage are merge prerequisites. Linked suites pass68/68 and46/46 cases. Typecheck and plain-directory acceptance pass. Preserve the failed broad local coverage attempt separately. Current Sentry gate, three explicit command spans, paired remote telemetry and local queue drainage are independently verified."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T18:03:48.746Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full-review remediation: reproduce required-root ordering and oversized-edge suppression before fixing the kernel; preserve deterministic continuation with a revised packing fingerprint. Hosted static identified generic machine-home paths in newly added performance evidence. Preview and apply the supported literal history redaction, retaining the audited chain, rather than editing generated history. Append corrections for two inaccurate maintenance statements. The user explicitly requested the GitHub/security/dependency/release inventory, so its canonical PM evidence stays in this reviewed delivery."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T18:07:26.388Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Verified CodeRabbit packing findings: unchanged first-head tests now fail three new assertions (required root endpoint ordering, feasible edge after an oversized edge, and Markdown detail bounds). The updated kernel prioritizes direct prerequisite/ancestor endpoints, keeps that order for producer cursors under a versioned fingerprint, and continues past an oversized edge. PM history redaction preview and apply each report zero hash mismatches, with a new audited redaction marker. Live nightly metadata confirms its measurement owner was already closed; both inaccurate maintenance statements have explicit corrective comments."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T18:09:39.107Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The review counterexamples fail3/5 cases before remediation. With the fixes, the new5-case integration file and41-case dependency suite pass46/46, and the unchanged graph-history/context suites previously pass24+43 cases. One legacy ordering assertion is intentionally updated to put the parent ahead of dependent context. Full tracker corrections use appended comments; generic environment paths are redacted through the audited CLI with verify_ok true and zero hash mismatches. No source or policy thresholds changed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T18:12:14.517Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final review-remediation linked tests pass70/70 graph/dependency cases and48/48 context cases (113 distinct). Typecheck, focused ESLint, SDK surface and documentation-link gates pass. New regressions cover priority before a lexically earlier descendant, cursor continuity and old-policy rejection, a feasible root edge after an oversized edge, and bounded Markdown failure details with exact counters. Corrective metadata and history-redaction audit remain in the same PR. Hosted static/coverage and the new full review are still required before merge."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T16:54:01.451Z","harness:codex","Packing policy: direct endpoints remain in breadth-first producer order. Reserve their root-edge token costs before admitting more distant nodes and emit root-incident edges first. Tiny accepted packets and explicit edge/depth caps may still omit relationships; completeness and producer-bounds omission receipts must remain visible. Do not equate a full field projection with an unbounded traversal."
  "2026-10-21T17:33:48.823Z","harness:codex",Graph preflight linked the historical dependency-context comparison and the actual startup-admission investigation as related work. The unrelated GitHub issue census points directly to its already-reviewed PR instead of inventing an implementation relationship. The graph policy and exemption ledger are unchanged.
